//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// House - First Impressions Dialogue

title: ApproachingHouse
---
<<play_emote player_emote drop>>

Dawn: No wonder Grams never told me about this place.
Dawn: Well, I'm pretty sure this is what she left me in the will. It’s gonna be a fixer upper, though.
===



//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Spirit 1st Dialogue

title: FirstSpiritIntro
---
// Variables ---------------------------------------------
<<declare $spiritExplained = false>>

// Dialogue Jumper ---------------------------------------
<<declare $spiritTalkTo = 0>>

<<if $spiritTalkTo == 1>>
    <<jump SpiritFiller1>>
<<elseif $spiritTalkTo == 2>>
    <<jump finishedIntroMinigame>>
<<endif>>
//---------------------------------------


<<set $spiritTalkTo = 1>>
<<play_cutscene PlayerCutsceneAnimator character_scared>>
<<play_cutscene CutsceneAnimator spirit-appear>>
<<play_emote_plain player_emote exclaim>>
Dawn: It that a… <shake>ghost?!</shake>
Dawn: Nup, nope, I’m out of here. Sorry Grams. <sketchy><b>This is just too much.<sketchy></b>.

Spirit: <shake>Wait, wait!</shake>
Spirit: Wow, it’s been a long time since I’ve seen a human here.
Spirit: Are you… wait, I know you. Or, at least, I think I do…
Spirit: Anne, is that you? You’ve gotten younger. And leaner.

Dawn: That’s my Grandma you’re talking about. My name's Dawn.

Spirit: Grandma? I didn’t think it had been <i>that</i> long.
Spirit: It’s nice to meet you, Dawn.
    -> It's nice to meet you too!
        <<play_cutscene PlayerCutsceneAnimator character_wave>>
        Dawn: Well it's a pleasure to meet you too... ghost?
        Spirit: Well, I'm spirit. Technically. But...
        <<set $spiritExplained to true>>
    -> What are you doing here?
        <<play_cutscene PlayerCutsceneAnimator character_scared>>
        Dawn: What are you doing in my Grandma's house?
        Spirit: I live here.
Spirit: She. This place. It’s been left alone so long, that all my friends have left. Now, it’s just me. 
Spirit: I don’t get why she would just leave us. This place broke down, and the spiritual energy with it.
Spirit: But, now you’re here, maybe you can help!

//Go through backstory and then come back
->So, you're a ghost...?
    <<detour spiritBackstory>>
->Okay, why are you <b>here</b>?
    <<detour spiritLocationBackstory>>
->Help, how?
    <<detour spiritHelp>>
//

Spirit: Anyways, we can make this a pleasant exchange! What were you planning to do here?

Dawn: I’ve been thinking I want to work in a cafe. I like cooking and making coffee, and I would like to meet some new people.

Spirit: Why don't we set up the old abandoned Cafe up again?
Spirit: And when more spirits come back, they can teach you some new recipes too! You see, we nature spirits kinda have a knack for these things.

Dawn: Wait, there’s gonna be more of you? Can’t it just be you?

Spirit: Don’t worry, they’re nice! Well, most. 
Spirit: When we start cleaning up and drawing more people to this spot, more of us will come home.

// Lead in to minigame
Dawn: Great.

Spirit: Now, let’s get to cooking! Your Grandma left a recipe book around here. I’ll grab it for you can I can teach you one of the recipes she loved to cook.
Spirit: Well how about you show us your skills by whipping me up a delicious plate of <wave>Waffles</wave>?

Dawn: You're kidding me right?

Spirit: Haha. No.
===
//
// 1st Dialogue Lead-Offs -------------------------------------------------------
//
title: spiritBackstory
---
    Dawn: So, you're a ghost haunting my grandma's House?

    <<if $spiritExplained == true>>
        Spirit: We've been over this already.
    <<endif>>

    Spirit: I’m not a ghost. More a <wave>“spirit of nature”</wave>.
    Spirit: And in regards to haunting; I'm far too <wave>cute</wave> to participate in such <sketchy>dubious</sketchy> activities.

    Dawn: A "spirit of nature"? What's that?

    Spirit: We are mediators between people and nature! Well used to be...
    
===
//
//
title: spiritLocationBackstory
---
Dawn: What are you doing in Grams' house?

Spirit: Well. I live here! Long ago, this town was a place of strong spiritual energy.
Spirit: And nothing gets the flames going like a little spiritual energy.
Spirit: But this place is long past its glory days, and that’s why the spirits who lived here left - more mould and mildew, less spiritual buzz, y’know.

Dawn: Ah, I don’t mean to sound rude, but do you have to live here? I don’t want little spirits hovering around me whilst I try and put my life back together.

Spirit: Spirits need these spaces. They remind us of who we are, and they help us connect with humans so we don’t become lost. And when we’re lost, we get… <wave>haunting</wave>.
===
//
//
title: spiritHelp
---
Dawn: You want my help? Why?

Spirit: Long ago, this town was a place of strong spiritual energy.
Spirit: We lived happily and Anne took care of us.
Spirit: Over time, people just forgot about us...

Dawn: Oh.
Spirit: We need your help bringing spiritual energy back into this place - will you help us?

Dawn: I'll consider it, little greenie.
===



//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Filler Dialogue - After 1st Dialogue

title:SpiritFiller1
---
Spirit: Once you've gotten those ingredients, I can teach you the recipe!
===



//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Spirit Tranformation Dialogue

title: finishedIntroMinigame
---
Spirit: Oh my! That looks <wave>delicious</wave>!
Dawn: See? Easy.
Spirit: Mmmm! It tastes amazing!
<<play_cutscene CutsceneAnimator seapancake-appear>>
Spirit: Oh golly gosh! I look so hotty hot.
Spirit: I bet you just wanna eat me all up.
<<view_model ModelViewerUI waffle>>
===



//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Spirit "Breakfast Toast" Cooking Dialogue

title: tutorialMainMinigame
---
Spirit: Dawn, its time to cook!
Spirit: But first you need to prep those tomatos.
Spirit: Use <sprite=1> to cut the tomatos.
===

title: CompletedCutting
---
Spirit: Good job!
Spirit: Now use [m1/] to drag the tomato cuts onto the tray.
Spirit: Then we can begin the cooking process!
===

title: CookingBacon
---
Spirit: Nice work!
Spirit: Before cooking you must drag the olive oil onto the grill.
Spirit: <sprite=1> to pour the oil onto the grill.
Spirit: Be sure to keep topping up the oil.
Spirit: Use [m1/] to drag the food onto the grill.
Spirit: When the food is cooked use <sprite=1> to flip the food.
Spirit: After the food is cooked, place it onto the tray.
===

title: Plating
---
Spirit: Nice!
Spirit: Now place all the food onto the tray!
Spirit: Then ring the bell to finish.
===

















